   * Organization settings including currency, timezone, and fiscal year start month are included in the response through a join with the organization settings table. Logo images are also included when available.
   *
   * Access to this endpoint is restricted based on user roles and organization membership. Admin users can view organizations within their organization context, while member users can only view organizations they belong to. Multi-tenancy isolation is enforced to ensure users cannot access data from organizations they are not members of.
   *
   * This operation is typically used in organization selection interfaces, multi-organization management dashboards, and organization context switching workflows.
   *
   * @param connection
   * @param body Search criteria, filters, and pagination parameters for organization listing
   * @x-autobe-authorization-type null
   * @x-autobe-authorization-actor null
   * @x-autobe-specification Query hrm_platform_organizations table with pagination and filtering support.
   *
   * 1. Apply search filter on organization name field using case-insensitive partial match
   * 2. Filter by organization status (active vs soft-deleted) based on deleted_at column
   * 3. Apply pagination using cursor-based or offset-based approach
   * 4. Support sorting by created_at, updated_at, or name fields
   * 5. Join with hrm_platform_organization_settings to include currency, timezone, and fiscal_year_start_month
   * 6. Join with hrm_platform_organization_logos to include logo image_url
   * 7. Apply role-based access control - only return organizations the authenticated user belongs to
   * 8. For admin users, return organizations within their organization context
   * 9. For member users, return organizations they have membership in
   * 10. Return total count for pagination metadata
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Patch()
  public async index(
    @TypedBody()
    body: IHrmPlatformOrganization.IRequest,
  ): Promise<IPageIHrmPlatformOrganization.ISummary> {
    try {
      return await patchHrmPlatformOrganizations({
        body,
      });
    } catch (error) {
      console.log(error);
      throw error;
    }
  }

  /**
   * Retrieve detailed information about a specific organization by its unique identifier.
   *
   * This operation returns comprehensive organization data including the organization name, optional description, owner reference, and creation/update timestamps. The organization serves as the primary business container within the platform, representing a distinct company or business unit that operates independently with complete data isolation from other organizations.
   *
   * The organization entity is the fundamental multi-tenancy boundary in the system. All employees, projects, tasks, time tracking data, and business operations are scoped to their respective organizations. This endpoint provides access to organization metadata that establishes the context for all organization-scoped operations.
   *
   * Access to this endpoint is restricted to authenticated members and administrators who have been assigned to the target organization. Users cannot access organization data from organizations they do not belong to, ensuring strict multi-tenancy isolation.
   *
