   * 2. Retrieve the project by projectId, ensuring it belongs to the current organization
   * 3. Verify the project exists and is accessible to the user
   * 4. Create a new snapshot record with:
   *    - Generate new UUID for snapshot id
   *    - Set project_id to the target project's id
   *    - Set hrm_platform_organization_id from the project's organization
   *    - Set created_by_id to the authenticated member's id
   *    - Copy all project fields (code, name, description, status, color_code, budget_hours) to snapshot
   *    - Set created_at to current timestamp
   * 5. Insert the snapshot into hrm_platform_project_snapshots table
   * 6. Record the snapshot creation action in the activity log with details (project id, snapshot id, creator)
   * 7. Return the created snapshot with all fields
   *
   * Validation rules:
   * - Project must exist and belong to the user's organization
   * - User must have project management permission
   * - Project must not be soft-deleted (deleted_at is null)
   * - Snapshot creation is idempotent - multiple snapshots of the same project are allowed
   *
   * Error handling:
   * - Return 404 if project not found
   * - Return 403 if user lacks permission
   * - Return 400 if project is deleted
   * @nestia Generated by Nestia - https://github.com/samchon/nestia
   */
  @TypedRoute.Post()
  public async createSnapshot(
    @MemberAuth()
    member: MemberPayload,
    @TypedParam("projectId")
    projectId: string & tags.Format<"uuid">,
